\section{UPACC-ES Validation Dataset Specification}
\subsection{Record Structure}

Each telemetry record $R_t$ is generated at solver step $t$ and binds
non-hydrostatic Navier--Stokes state variables to cryptographic and
control-law performance metrics. The formal schema is:

\[
R_t = 
\left\{
\begin{aligned}
& t && \text{(solver step index)} \\
& u_{\max}(t) && \text{peak velocity magnitude from } \mathbf{u}(x,y,z,t) \\
& Y_{\text{global}}(t) && \text{global yield index (triad p-norm)} \\
& \Delta t_{\text{master}}(t) && \text{active sovereign timestep} \\
& R_{\text{fluid}}(t) && \text{fluid Courant ratio} \\
& R_{\text{crypto}}(t) && \text{crypto timing ratio} \\
& R_{\text{volatile}}(t) && \text{volatile ingest ratio} \\
& \tau_{\text{crypto}}(t) && \text{AES-GCM-256 hardware latency (ms)} \\
& S_{\text{PEK}}(t) && \text{cryptographic validation status} \\
\end{aligned}
\right\}
\]

\subsection{Global Yield Index}
\[
Y_{\text{global}}(t)
=
\left(
R_{\text{fluid}}(t)^6
+
R_{\text{crypto}}(t)^6
+
R_{\text{volatile}}(t)^6
\right)^{1/6}.
\]

\subsection{Lyapunov Autothrottle Update}
\[
\Delta t_{\text{master}}(t+1)
=
\Delta t_{\text{master}}(t)
\left[
1 + K_p\left(Y_{\text{target}} - Y_{\text{global}}(t)\right)
\right].
\]

\subsection{Dataset Export}
All records $R_t$ are appended to a persistent JSON corpus for
long-horizon spectral analysis, stability verification, and publication.

